{
  "_version": "1.0.0",
  "_description": "Box admin-events log → AKSI control ID mapping. Box (https://box.com) is the leading enterprise content management platform — heavily adopted by regulated industries (healthcare, financial services, legal). Agents now read, write, and share Box content at scale, and Box's /2.0/events?stream_type=admin_logs feed surfaces the data-loss-prevention signals that govern enterprise file storage: downloads, uploads, deletions, sharing transitions (link access, expiration), collaboration invites, role changes, DLP-violation hits, watermark labels, Box Shield anomaly alerts, malware detection, device-trust failures, and login events. Box's event_type drives the primary control. Agent activity (actor_type=service_account/app) downloading sensitive-extension files is a top-tier review signal. Public-unprotected shared links and DLP violations are the dominant exfiltration vector and resolve to DE-01 / PR-04 FAIL. Bulk-download and cross-folder traversal patterns produce synthetic PR-04 FAIL/FLAG.",
